# R11: warm ADMA2 read of LBA1 in the bootloader's 8-bit/HS400 state.
#
# boot-irq60 confirmed the minutes-later black screen was the UEFI/PMIC charger
# watchdog: EnableChargerWdog=0 and the same XNU kernel stayed alive.  boot-irq59's
# photo then showed what the bootloader actually left:
#
#   HC1 = 0x38       8-bit bus + ADMA2 64-bit
#   HC2 = 0x0003     V4EN=0, v3 register layout
#   CLK = 0x0007     divider 0, ~100 MHz
#   VS  = 0x240a0e   HS400 select-in + DLL active
#   PS  = 0x01f800f0 card inserted, CMD/DAT high, no inhibit
#
# irq58 tried a warm SDMA read from this state, cleared the ADMA64 DMA select and
# did SWRST_DAT; that is a different engine/timing and black-screened.  This patch
# keeps the boot state exactly:
#
#   - enable the GCC gates first (idempotent, no card-state change);
#   - publish HC1/HC2/CLK/PS/VSPEC on the stage lines;
#   - CMD13 on RCA 1, require Transfer with no error;
#   - one CMD17 LBA1 through a 16-byte ADMA2 descriptor next to the page-aligned
#     bounce buffer, with HC1/clock/VSPEC/DLL untouched and no SWRST_DAT;
#   - EFI PART -> keep the state, set su.adma and parse the GPT with ADMA2 reads;
#     anything else -> return to the ordinary v3 re-identification path.
#
# Panel row 3 is shortened back to v4/hc1/hc2/w/bs/bc/sdm/ok/st/de so st and de
# stay inside the panel; ps/clk/vs ride the stage text.
